// endpoint_get_shell_run_claims.proto — GetShellRunClaims: WHICH RUN each of a
// set of vendor task ids names, and which book holds that run's launching call.
//
// WHY THE SIDECAR ASKS. A detached shell's spool is named by the vendor's task
// id, and the sidecar reads a spool only once a spawning call claims it. The
// transcript states the claim in a structured field for most launches, but a
// shell the vendor moved to the background on its own timeout inside a
// subagent is stated only in prose, and a spool nothing claimed is never read:
// its terminal is never seen and the run stays live forever. The vendor's task
// stream states the pairing for every run, and the shim, which reads that
// stream, writes it (EntryBatch.shell_run_claims).
//
// WHY THE BOOK COMES FROM THE STORE. The shim does not always know which agent
// made the launching call (a backgrounded subagent's calls never reach its
// stream), but the call's own activity row is on record in exactly that book,
// written by whichever producer read the call. So the store answers the book
// from the row, and a run whose call is not on record yet is answered without
// one: the sidecar holds the spool and asks again.
//
// UNSCOPED ON PURPOSE. The sidecar reads every session on the host; a task id
// is the vendor's own name and is compared for equality only.

